<main id="main">
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Point of sale and back office</p>
      <h1>The register, the stock room and the books. One place.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Rupert runs the counter and everything behind it: ring up sales, keep stock right across your stores, close the day and hand your bookkeeper numbers that already match.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="https://rupertpos.com/start">Create free account</a>
        <a class="button quiet" href="#pricing">See pricing</a>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Google sign-in · No card needed to create an account</p>
    </div>

    <div class="preview" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative preview of Rupert: today's sales and stock across two stores, the day close status, and a sale on the register">
      <div class="panel today">
        <div class="panel-head"><strong>Today</strong><span>2 stores</span></div>
        <div class="tiles">
          <div class="tile"><small>Sales</small><b>$2,418</b></div>
          <div class="tile"><small>Low stock</small><b>6 items</b></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="rows">
          <li><span>Main St close</span><span class="ok">Balanced</span></li>
          <li><span>Warehouse close</span><span class="warn">1 to review</span></li>
          <li><span>On the clock</span><span>5 staff</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel ticket">
        <div class="panel-head"><strong>Register 1</strong><span>Main St</span></div>
        <ul class="rows">
          <li><span>Lavender tincture</span><span>$34.00</span></li>
          <li><span>Calm tea × 2</span><span>$18.00</span></li>
          <li class="total"><span>Total</span><span>$52.00</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tenders"><span class="tender primary">Card</span><span class="tender">Cash</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note caption">Illustrative preview. Available features and provider readiness vary.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="product">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What Rupert does</p>
      <h2>Four jobs, one workspace.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Most shops juggle a register app, a stock spreadsheet, a timesheet tool and a bookkeeper's inbox. Rupert puts them in one place, so each sale moves the stock, the drawer and the books together.</p>
      <div class="pillars">
        <article class="pillar">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 7h16v10H4z"/><path d="M8 11h3M8 14h8"/><path d="M7 7V4h10v3"/></svg>
          </span>
          <h3>Sell</h3>
          <p>A full-screen register for the counter.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Cash and card tenders, tips and receipts</li>
            <li>Registers, customers and every channel's sales</li>
            <li>Online and in-store orders side by side</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 8l8-4 8 4v8l-8 4-8-4z"/><path d="M4 8l8 4 8-4M12 12v8"/></svg>
          </span>
          <h3>Stock</h3>
          <p>One count of what you have, in every store.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Inventory by location and store comparison</li>
            <li>Physical counts, transfers and stock alerts</li>
            <li>Purchase orders, vendors and bulk recipes</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 4h12v16H6z"/><path d="M9 8h6M9 12h6M9 16h3"/></svg>
          </span>
          <h3>Books</h3>
          <p>Closing the day keeps the books.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Day close and daily reconciliation</li>
            <li>General ledger, expenses and bank reconciliation</li>
            <li>Statements, sales tax, cash flow and forecasts</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="9" cy="9" r="3"/><circle cx="17" cy="10" r="2.4"/><path d="M3.5 19c.8-3 3-4.5 5.5-4.5s4.7 1.5 5.5 4.5M15 15.2c2.3-.3 4.6.9 5.5 3.8"/></svg>
          </span>
          <h3>Team</h3>
          <p>Who is working, and what they are owed.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Time clock, timesheets and shifts</li>
            <li>Leave, PTO and pay runs</li>
            <li>Team chat and training progress</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="day">
    <p class="eyebrow">How a day runs</p>
    <h2>From opening the drawer to closing the books.</h2>
    <ol class="day">
      <li><span class="step">Open</span><h3>Start the register.</h3><p>Count the drawer and open a register for the shift.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step">Sell</span><h3>Ring it up.</h3><p>Sales at the counter and from connected stores land in one list.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step">Stock</span><h3>Stock follows.</h3><p>Each sale moves the count. Low items show up before the shelf is empty.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step">Close</span><h3>Close the day.</h3><p>Rupert checks the register against cash and card deposits and flags what does not match.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step">Books</span><h3>Hand off clean books.</h3><p>Closed days post to the ledger for your bookkeeper to review and approve.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="connections">
    <div class="wrap connect">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Works with what you have</p>
        <h2>Keep your tools. Connect them here.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">Bring in sales, items and hours from the systems you already run. Each connection is set up and authorized separately in your workspace, and signing in to Rupert never connects anything on its own.</p>
        <a class="link" href="https://techmore.github.io/rupert/overview.html">See what each connection supports →</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="logos" aria-label="Supported connections">
        <li>Shopify</li>
        <li>Square</li>
        <li>C-Trax</li>
        <li>SwipeSimple</li>
        <li>QuickBooks import</li>
        <li>Google Drive copies</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="pricing">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
    <h2>Start free. Subscribe when you are ready.</h2>
    <div class="pricing">
      <article class="plan">
        <h3>Free account</h3>
        <div class="price">$0</div>
        <p>Google sign-in and your own workspace. Start using the system and connect providers when you are ready.</p>
        <p class="note">Provider-specific credentials and setup may be required.</p>
        <a class="button quiet" href="https://rupertpos.com/start">Create free account</a>
      </article>
      <article class="plan">
        <h3>Monthly</h3>
        <div class="price">$499 <small>USD / month</small></div>
        <p>A recurring Rupert subscription, billed monthly through Stripe.</p>
        <p class="note">Taxes may apply. Billing by CSP Cyber Security Pilot.</p>
        <a class="button quiet" href="https://rupertpos.com/billing">Choose monthly</a>
      </article>
      <article class="plan featured">
        <span class="badge">Referred by a customer</span>
        <h3>Referral</h3>
        <div class="price">$249.50 <small>USD / month</small></div>
        <p>50% off for the first 12 months with an eligible customer referral code and a 12-month commitment.</p>
        <p class="note">$2,994 total commitment before tax, billed monthly. Then $499/month. Verify your code in your workspace.</p>
        <a class="button" href="https://rupertpos.com/billing">Use a referral code</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap trust">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Customer permission comes first</p>
        <h2>Support when you want it. Access you control.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Connecting a provider and granting Rupert support access are separate decisions. Choose a support administrator, grant temporary read access and revoke it from your workspace.</p>
        <p class="note">Saved provider credentials are encrypted on the server. Customer-held encryption keys are planned; current encryption does not prevent access by infrastructure operators.</p>
        <a class="link" href="https://rupertpos.com/support-access">Manage support permissions →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section faq">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2>Before you get started.</h2>
    <details><summary>Do I need a card to sign up?</summary><p>No. Create your account with a verified Google identity. Paid checkout is a separate step inside your workspace.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How does the referral discount work?</summary><p>An active paying Rupert customer can share their referral code. Eligible new subscriptions receive 50% off the $499 monthly price for 12 months in exchange for a 12-month commitment. You pay $249.50 per month, then $499 per month after the first year. Taxes may apply.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Who bills my subscription?</summary><p>Stripe processes subscription payments using the CSP Cyber Security Pilot billing account. You review the amount before confirming payment.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Google sign-in connect all my business accounts?</summary><p>No. It verifies your identity for Rupert. Each supported provider connection needs its own authorization and setup.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where can I check current capabilities?</summary><p>Read the <a href="https://techmore.github.io/rupert/overview.html">feature overview</a> and <a href="https://techmore.github.io/rupert/roadmap.html">roadmap</a> for implemented, partial and planned functionality.</p></details>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap closing">
    <h2>Open your workspace today.</h2>
    <p>Free to start. No card needed.</p>
    <a class="button" href="https://rupertpos.com/start">Create free account</a>
  </section>
</main>

